        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Traefik, an HTTP reverse proxy and load balancer. When the `headerField` is configured with a non-canonical HTTP header name, an authenticated attacker can inject a canonical version of that header. This allows the attacker to impersonate any identity to the backend, leading to an authentication bypass. The backend prioritizes the attacker-injected header, overriding Traefik's intended header.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "github.com/traefik/traefik: Traefik: Authentication bypass via non-canonical HTTP header injection",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
